From 1f33ade034ab7ff5d4c5c64e0f80f4297c9b0920 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ththeod <2376818+ththeod@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 14:01:34 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 118/138] Sparse logits gather, int8 DFlash 2 candidate head,
 FlashInfer top-k-first sampler (all opt-in)

- VLLM_EXP_SPARSE_LOGITS=1: when every scheduled request has top_k <= 64, no
  logprobs, no penalties / logit bias / bad words / thinking budget, and no
  grammar, the target's logits are gathered as each TP shard's top-64
  (FlashInfer radix top-k) scattered into -inf (LogitsProcessor.
  get_sparse_logits, Qwen4Exp compute_logits_sparse, Sampler.sparse_logits_ok).
  After the sampler's top-k/top-p the logits equal the full gather (W27 test).
- VLLM_EXP_DRAFT_HEAD_INT8=1: per-row int8 copy of the LM head shard (303 MiB on
  the last PP stage) for DFlash 2 candidate selection only, W8A16 skinny kernel
  (373 us vs 731 us bf16 at 8 rows); top-16 overlap with the bf16 head 1.00 / 0.98.
- VLLM_EXP_TOPK_FIRST=1 now uses FlashInfer's radix top-k (~80 us for 8 x 248K)
  instead of torch.topk.

W28 profile at 1 request vs p7 (W26): last-stage work per step 11.60 -> 11.07 ms,
step period 20.80 -> 20.59 ms (first stage varies with sampled content); kernel
view: int8 head -357 us, logits all-gather -196 us, sampler -176 us per step.
GSM8K 97.5 (121 s, 491 tok/s), probes/poke clean, 0 runtime errors.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
